      "text": "$83$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\frac{x}{-c}+\\frac{y}{-c / b}=1$<br/><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/eDsv3X9dN5TI8V0dK04gBDTsdlL5b5Qh_0aP9jYVS8Q.original.fullsize.png\"/><br/>$\\begin{aligned} & \\therefore \\text { area of triangle }=\\frac{1}{2}\\left|\\frac{c^2}{b}\\right|=48 \\\\ & \\left|\\frac{c^2}{b}\\right|=96 \\\\ & \\because-c=-\\frac{c}{b} \\\\ & \\Rightarrow b=1 \\quad \\therefore c^2=96 \\\\ & \\therefore b^2+c^2=97\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
